    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nMoved all date-derived owner values onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by its ending calendar year \u2014 the standard Australian convention this app already leans into).\n\n**New single source of truth** \u2014 `util/FiscalYear.java`\nOwns the fiscal-year definition so the three concerns stay in step, mirroring the existing `CustomerCode`/`AgeBand` helper style:\n- `of(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year a date falls in (its ending calendar year)\n- `labelOf(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` label\n- `shortYearOf(date)` \u2014 the two-digit year segment\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed\n\n**`fiscalYear` response field**\n- Added a derived `getFiscalYear()` to `Owner` (returns `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted registration date; `null` when no date).\n- Added the `fiscalYear` property to the OpenAPI `Owner` schema; MapStruct maps it automatically by name \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\n**Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`\nNow takes `<YY>` from `FiscalYear.shortYearOf(registrationDate)` instead of the raw calendar year (e.g. a 21 Sept 2026 registration now yields `...-M27`, since it's in FY ending 2027).\n\n**Tenure** \u2014 `Owner`\nReplaced `getTenureDays()` (a 365-day window via `ChronoUnit.DAYS`) with `getTenureFiscalYears()` using `FiscalYear.elapsed(...)`; membership points now award +3 once at least one fiscal year has elapsed. A newly created owner still has zero tenure, so it earns no tenure points at creation.\n\nDescriptions in `openapi.yml` were updated to match, and I added `FiscalYearTest` covering the July boundary, labels, and elapsed-year counting.\n\n## Test status\n- `mvn test` \u2014 **green**: 16/16 (`FiscalYearTest`, `BusinessDaysTest`, `AcceptanceTest` incl. the `fiscalYear` acceptance check).\n- One note: `mvn verify` fails its JaCoCo gate (0.23 global line coverage vs. 0.85 expected). This is a **pre-existing baseline** \u2014 the repo ships only 8 tests for the whole codebase, so the gate cannot pass regardless of this change; my additions don't regress it. The test suite itself is green.",
